l compliance feature for biometric systems (what we ship)\n- Proposal 3: Operational/data governance program for long-term log stewardship (how we maintain over time)\n\nNow let me draft each proposal at 60-110 words total across four fields.\n\nLet me count carefully.\n\nProposal 1: \"Embed Automatic Logging into the R&D Pipeline\"\n- title: Embed Logging Architecture into Core R&D Workflow (8 words - good, under 10)\n- what: A mandatory engineering standard that requires every high-risk AI prototype to include an event-recording layer from the first sprint, capturing risk-relevant events and operational data in a structured, queryable format.\n- how: The compliance team drafts a technical specification aligned with Article 12(2)(a)-(c); the platform engineering group builds a shared logging middleware; R&D project leads integrate it during design reviews before any model is deployed to testing.\n- why: Building traceability in from inception avoids costly retrofits and demonstrates to regulators that compliance is structural, not cosmetic, protecting the lab's market reputation.\n\nLet me count words: \ntitle: \"Embed Logging Architecture into Core R&D Workflow\" = 8 words (not counted in the 60-110? Let me re-read... \"Keep each proposal between 60 and 110 words across its four fields.\" So title, what, how, why combined should be 60-110 words.)\n\nLet me recount:\ntitle: Embed(1) Logging(2) Architecture(3) into(4) Core(5) R&D(6) Workflow(7) = 7 words\nwhat: A(1) mandatory(2) engineering(3) standard(4) that(5) requires(6) every(7) high-risk(8) AI(9) prototype(10) to(11) include(12) an(13) event-recording(14) layer(15) from(16) the(17) first(18) sprint,(19) capturing(20) risk-relevant(21) events(22) and(23) operational(24) data(25) in(26) a(27) structured,(28) queryable(29) format.(30) = 30 words\nhow: The(1) compliance(2) team(3) drafts(4) a(5) technical(6) specification(7) aligned(8) with(9) Article(10) 12(2)(a)-(c);(11) the(12) platform(13) engineering(14) group(15) builds(16) a(17) shared(18) logging(19) middleware;(20) R&D(21) project(22) leads(23) integrate(24) it(25) during(26) design(27) reviews(28) before(29) any(30) model(31) is(32) deployed(33) to(34) testing.(35) = 35 words\nwhy: Building(1) traceability(2) in(3) from(4) inception(5) avoids(6) costly(7) retrofits(8) and(9) demonstrates(10) to(11) regulators(12) that(13) compliance(14) is(15) structural,(16) not(17) cosmetic,(18) protecting(19) the(20) lab's(21) market(22) reputation.(23) = 23 words\n\nTotal: 7 + 30 + 35 + 23 = 95 words. Good, within 60-110.\n\nProposal 2: \"Biometric Verification and Match-Logging Module\"\n- title: Annex III Biometric Logging Compliance Module (7 words)\n- what: A purpose-built software component for any system falling under Annex III point 1(a) that automatically captures start/end timestamps, the reference database used, matched input data, and the identity of verifying natural persons per Article 14(5).\n- how: The team scopes a dedicated logging service with tamper-evident storage; QA writes test cases mapping each of the four minimum fields to real verification workflows; legal reviews retention policies against Member State data-protection rules.\n- why: This closes the most prescriptive gap in the regulation for our biometric products and prevents enforcement action that could halt commercial deployments entirely.\n\nLet me count:\ntitle: Annex(1) III(2) Biometric(3) Logging(4) Compliance(5) Module(6) = 6 words\nwhat: A(1) purpose-built(2) software(3) component(4) for(5) any(6) system(7) falling(8) under(9) Annex(10) III(11) point(12) 1(a)(13) that(14) automatically(15) captures(16) start/end(17) timestamps,(18) the(19) reference(20) database(21) used,(22) matched(23) input(24) data,(25) and(26) the(27) identity(28) of(29) verifying(30) natural(31) persons(32) per(33) Article(34) 14(5).(35) = 35 words\nhow: The(1) team(2) scopes(3) a(4) dedicated(5) logging(6) service(7) with(8) tamper-evident(9) storage;(10) QA(11) write