ab's internal compliance policy.\nWhy: Biometric systems attract the sharpest regulatory scrutiny; catching log gaps before an authority does preserves our operating licence and public trust.\n\nLet me count:\nTitle: Biometric-System Log Audit Programme for Annex III Compliance \nWhat: Because(1) Article(2) 12(3)(3) imposes(4) specific(5) minimum(6) logging(7) fields(8) on(9) biometric(10) identification(11) and(12) verification(13) systems(14), I(15) will(16) stand(17) up(18) a(19) dedicated(20) quarterly(21) audit(22) that(23) samples(24) production(25) logs(26) against(27) those(28) four(29) mandatory(30) elements(31). This(32) is(33) distinct(34) from(35) general(36) engineering(37) because(38) it(39) addresses(40) the(41) most(42) prescriptive(43) sub-category(44) of(45) the(46) Act(47). = 47 words\n\nHow: We(1) will(2) build(3) an(4) automated(5) log-verification(6) script(7) that(8) flags(9) any(10) session(11) record(12) missing(13) any(14) of(15) the(16) four(17) Article(18) 12(3)(19) fields(20), run(21) it(22) weekly(23) against(24) our(25) biometric(26) product(27) lines(28), and(29) escalate(30) gaps(31) to(32) engineering(33) within(34) five(35) business(36) days(37) under(38) a(39) remediation(40) SLA(41) I(42) am(43) writing(44) into(45) the(46) lab's(47) internal(48) compliance(49) policy(50). = 50 words\n\nWhy: Biometric(1) systems(2) attract(3) the(4) sharpest(5) regulatory(6) scrutiny(7); catching(8) log(9) gaps(10) before(11) an(12) authority(13) does(14) preserves(15) our(16) operating(17) licence(18) and(19) public(20) trust(21). = 21 words\n\nTotal: 7 + 47 + 50 + 21 = 125. Too long. Need to trim about 15-20 words.\n\nLet me revise:\nTitle: Biometric Log Audit for Annex III Minimum Fields \nWhat: Article 12(3) mandates four specific log fields for biometric systems—timestamps, reference database, matched input, verifier identity. I will run a dedicated quarterly audit sampling production logs against those elements, distinct from general engine