owledge about AI system longevity that no single company would voluntarily produce, positioning our lab at the frontier of trustworthy-AI science.\"\n},\n{\n\"title\": \"Open Logging Schema for Reproducible AI Research\",\n\"what\": \"We design and publish a versioned, open logging specification that satisfies Article 12 minimums while also capturing scientifically meaningful metadata such as hyperparameter trajectories, intermediate loss values, and calibration metrics.\",\n\"how\": \"A small interdisciplinary team of researchers and engineers drafts the schema over two sprints, validates it against our biometric pipeline in a pilot deployment, then releases it under an open licence with documentation targeting both auditors and peer reviewers.\",\n\"why\": \"It elevates our intellectual standing by setting field-wide methodological norms for how AI evidence is recorded, making our lab the reference point for reproducible high-risk development.\"\n},\n{\n\"title\": \"Sandbox Protocol for Unlogged Exploratory Research\",\n\"what\": \"We draft an internal classification framework that distinguishes exploratory research (pre-intended-purpose, no real-world deployment) from regulated high-risk operation, so novel experimental work is not prematurely burdened with full logging infrastructure.\",\n\"how\": \"In consultation with the compliance officer, we define concrete thresholds such as data volume, user exposure, and decision stakes at which a prototype crosses into Article 12 scope, and build a lightweight metadata capture layer that scales up to full logging only at that boundary.\",\n\"why\": \"It preserves our lab's capacity to pursue uncertain, high-risk intellectual directions without the overhead of compliance architecture strangling early-stage discovery.\"\n}\n]\n}",
