rch Pipelines\",\n\"what\": \"An open-source specification and reference implementation for structured event logs in AI development pipelines, designed to satisfy Article 12 requirements so any lab or company can adopt it without bespoke engineering.\",\n\"how\": \"We prototype the schema on two of our own high-risk prototypes—a biometric verification model per Annex III point 1(a) and a post-market monitoring dashboard—then publish it under an MIT licence with conformance test suites.\",\n\"why\": \"It creates shared scientific infrastructure that reduces duplication across the EU research community and positions the lab as a standard-setter rather than merely a rule-follower.\"\n},\n{\n\"title\": \"Drift-Detection Science from Lifetime Event Streams\",\n\"what\": \"A research programme investigating statistical and machine-learning methods for detecting performance degradation, distributional shift, or novel risk emergence in deployed high-risk systems using only the automatically recorded event logs mandated by Article 12(1).\",\n\"how\": \"We build a benchmark of synthetic drift scenarios across model families, evaluate detection algorithms under realistic log-sparsity constraints, and publish the results as open benchmarks with fully reproducible harnesses.\",\n\"why\": \"It converts a compliance obligation into a genuine contribution to operational AI-safety science that the broader community can adopt well beyond EU jurisdiction.\"\n}\n]\n}",
