ntation Lifecycle and Post-Market Review Cadence\",\n\"what\": \"A standing governance process that keeps every high-risk system's technical documentation current throughout its lifetime and ties it to scheduled post-market monitoring reviews, as Recital 71 demands.\",\n\"how\": \"I would institute a quarterly documentation audit cycle led by my compliance office, with engineering owning content updates and a designated reviewer verifying alignment between live system behaviour and recorded capabilities, limitations, and risk-management descriptions.\",\n\"why\": \"Stale documentation is the fastest route to a regulatory finding that damages our market reputation and invites enforcement action.\"\n},\n{\n\"title\": \"Build Annex III Biometric-Specific Logging Compliance Module\",\n\"what\": \"A product-level feature set for any biometric identification system we develop that captures, at minimum, per-use timestamps, the reference database consulted, matched input data, and the identity of each natural person who verifies results under Article 14(5).\",\n\"how\": \"The applied-AI group would implement these four data fields as mandatory, non-disableable outputs in the biometric pipeline's inference layer, with read-only access granted to our compliance office for audit purposes.\",\n\"why\": \"Failing to meet the explicit minimums of Article 12(3) exposes us to immediate regulatory breach on a product category where enforcement is most visible.\"\n}\n]\n}",
