ture change to satisfy Article 12(1) and (2).\n\n2. **Process/Governance**: Establish a post-market monitoring and documentation lifecycle program. This addresses Recital 71's requirement for up-to-date technical documentation and Article 12(2)(b)-(c).\n\n3. **Product-specific compliance module**: For any Annex III point 1(a) systems (biometric identification), build the specific minimum logging features required by Article 12(3) - start/end times, reference database, input data matches, verification person IDs.\n\nLet me make sure these are genuinely different:\n- #1 is about building a general-purpose logging architecture into all high-risk AI systems (engineering/infrastructure)\n- #2 is about the documentation and monitoring governance process (organizational/process change)\n- #3 is about a specific product compliance feature set for biometric systems (product-level development task)\n\nThese are distinct: infrastructure, process/governance, and product-specific engineering.\n\nNow let me write each proposal keeping 60-110 words total across all four fields.\n\nLet me draft:\n\n**Proposal 1:**\n- title: Embed Auto-Logging Architecture in All High-Risk Pipelines (9 words - good)\n- what: A reusable logging middleware layer that automatically records system events throughout each high-risk AI model's operational lifetime, satisfying Article 12(1) and the traceability needs of paragraph 2.\n- how: The engineering team would integrate a standardized event-capture SDK into every deployment pipeline before next release cycle, with schema definitions covering risk-flagging triggers, post-market monitoring queries, and operational telemetry hooks.\n- why: Without this built-in from design, retrofitting logs later risks non-compliance and jeopardises our ability to serve EU clients at all.\n\nLet me count words: title is separate (not counted in the 60-110). Actually, re-reading the instructions: \"Keep each proposal between 60 and 110 words across its four fields.\" So