ance Schema and Capture Toolkit\",\n      \"what\": \"A concrete data schema plus a lightweight capture library that ensures Annex III point 1(a) systems automatically log session timestamps, reference-database identifiers, matched input records, and verifier identities as required by Article 12(3).\",\n      \"how\": \"We build the schema as a versioned JSON spec, wrap it in a thin SDK hooking into our biometric matching pipeline, and validate outputs against the four mandatory fields using automated contract tests on every prototype build.\",\n      \"why\": \"It converts four regulatory data points into a tested engineering artifact so prototyping teams stop guessing at compliance coverage.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"Compliance Checkpoint Gate in Prototype Sprint Cycle\",\n      \"what\": \"A mandatory mid-sprint stage where a designated engineer verifies the prototype's logging captures all events relevant to Article 12(2)(a) through (c) before integration testing begins. This catches traceability gaps while fixes are still cheap, not after architecture has hardened.\",\n      \"how\": \"We add a two-hour gate to our sprint cadence, backed by a clause-mapped checklist and a replay tool that simulates incident scenarios against the live log stream to confirm retrievability.\",\n      \"why\": \"It protects prototyping speed by front-loading compliance validation into the iteration loop rather than surfacing gaps at audit time.\"\n    }\n  ]\n}",
