igh-risk systems, and provides regulators a single standardised auditable artifact across our entire portfolio.\"\n},\n{\n\"title\": \"Living Technical Documentation Lifecycle Program\",\n\"what\": \"A structured internal program that treats technical documentation as a continuously maintained living artefact rather than a one-time pre-release deliverable, ensuring it tracks every algorithmic revision, data update, and performance shift across the system's full operational lifetime.\",\n\"how\": \"Dedicated documentation engineers are assigned to each high-risk product line and maintain versioned records of training-data provenance, validation outcomes, and risk-management decisions, with automated triggers that flag whenever a model or code change requires doc updates before deployment.\",\n\"why\": \"This directly satisfies Recital 71's mandate for up-to-date technical documentation and positions the lab as a transparent, auditable partner in the eyes of both national regulators and enterprise clients.\"\n},\n{\n\"title\": \"Post-Market Monitoring Analytics Research Line\",\n\"what\": \"A dedicated research track focused on developing methods for continuous operational monitoring and anomaly detection in deployed high-risk systems, producing the analytical capability needed to fulfil Article 12(2)(b) post-market monitoring obligations.\",\n\"how\": \"The lab assembles a small interdisciplinary team combining ML researchers with regulatory analysts to prototype drift-detection and risk-flagging pipelines that consume the automatic logs mandated by Article 12(1), generating actionable alerts before degradation escalates into safety incidents.\",\n\"why\": \"This converts a compliance obligation into an R&D differentiator, giving clients a monitoring service they cannot easily replicate while reducing our liability exposure from undetected system degradation in production.\"\n}\n]\n}",
