orithms, training data provenance, testing results, risk-management records—and the raw operational logs for each deployed system across its entire service life.\",\n\"how\": \"We deploy a document-and-log management platform integrated with our CI/CD pipeline; every deployment event auto-stamps a new version entry, and a dedicated compliance analyst performs quarterly integrity reviews of log completeness against Article 12(2) criteria.\",\n\"why\": \"Recital 71 demands documentation stay current throughout the system's lifetime, and a living archive is what lets us produce traceable evidence when a regulator opens an investigation or a customer files a complaint.\"\n},\n{\n\"title\": \"R&D Team Compliance Training on Logging Obligations\",\n\"what\": \"A recurring training-and-assessment programme for engineers and research leads that covers the specific logging requirements of Article 12, how to interpret events relevant under paragraphs 2(a) through (c), and what constitutes a reportable risk scenario triggering enhanced logging.\",\n\"how\": \"The compliance office co-designs half-day workshops with the engineering management team; each cohort must pass a practical exercise in which they trace a synthetic incident back through mock logs to identify the responsible verification step.\",\n\"why\": \"Our people are the first line of defence; if researchers do not internalise what must be captured, the technical architecture alone produces gaps that surface only during a regulator's post-market review.\"\n}\n]\n}",
