roject proposal, sized at eight to twelve percent of total effort, covering logging implementation, documentation upkeep, and post-market monitoring setup.\",\n      \"how\": \"I will revise our internal grant-review template so the R&D committee scores proposals on how efficiently they absorb this overhead by leveraging shared infrastructure rather than duplicating it per team.\",\n      \"why\": \"This keeps scientific ambition intact while making the true cost of compliance visible, preventing silent budget erosion across parallel projects competing for the same funding pool.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"Mine Compliance Logs as R&D Training Signals\",\n      \"what\": \"Repurpose the automatic event logs that Article 12 mandates into a longitudinal dataset of real-world system behaviour, edge cases, and failure modes accumulated across deployed models.\",\n      \"how\": \"Designate one research postdoc to build an analytics pipeline over the logging store, feeding anomaly patterns back into our model-iteration sprints as labelled training signals for robustness work.\",\n      \"why\": \"This turns a regulatory obligation into a scarce resource — real operational data expensive to collect otherwise — strengthening both compliance posture and scientific output from the same infrastructure spend.\"\n    }\n  ]\n}",
