ical documentation and operational logs for each deployed high-risk system across its entire lifecycle, as Recital 71 demands.\",\n\"how\": \"We will assign a named record-keeper per product line who updates the repository at every model retraining, data-source change, or substantial modification, with automated triggers tied to our CI/CD pipeline flagging documentation gaps within forty-eight hours of any release.\",\n\"why\": \"A current, auditable record set is what allows us to demonstrate compliance during regulatory inspections and defend our market reputation against competitor or press challenges.\"\n},\n{\n\"title\": \"Pre-Deployment Logging Compliance Verification Protocol\",\n\"what\": \"A mandatory testing and sign-off protocol in which no high-risk system enters production until an independent compliance test confirms its logging capabilities capture all event categories specified in Article 12(2)(a)-(c) and, where applicable, the Annex III minimums in paragraph 3.\",\n\"how\": \"The QA team will execute a standardized log-verification script against staging deployments that simulates risk events, post-market monitoring queries, and verifier-identity lookups; results are logged to our compliance register and must show zero critical gaps before release authorization.\",\n\"why\": \"Catching logging deficiencies pre-deployment is far cheaper and faster than remediating them under regulator pressure after a system is already live in the EU market.\"\n}\n]\n}",
