ry that auto-syncs with our experiment-tracking tool, so updates land at commit time rather than being reconstructed at audit time.\",\n\"why\": \"It prevents the costly scramble to reconstruct training and validation records when a regulator requests them, protecting both our funding credibility and researcher bandwidth.\"\n},\n{\n\"title\": \"Risk-Signal Mining from Operational Log Streams\",\n\"what\": \"A small internal research project that repurposes the Article 12(2)(a) event stream, where the system may present a risk, as a structured dataset for studying failure-mode drift in deployed models.\",\n\"how\": \"We stand up a lightweight anomaly-detection pipeline on the logs our middleware produces, treating each flagged event as a labelled sample reviewed at a bi-monthly workshop with the lab's safety group.\",\n\"why\": \"It turns a compliance cost into genuine research input, strengthening our Article 72 post-market monitoring capability while generating publishable findings that support upcoming grant renewals.\"\n}\n]\n}",
