er regulator.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"Pre-Registered Drift Hypotheses Embedded in Logging Protocols\",\n      \"what\": \"Treat each Article 12(2)(a)-(c) logging category as a pre-registered hypothesis about when and how our systems will exhibit risk-relevant drift, substantial modification, or performance degradation, turning compliance monitoring into structured experimental inquiry.\",\n      \"how\": \"Before any system enters the EU market, the responsible researcher files a one-page protocol specifying the null hypothesis, the log-derived statistic that would falsify it, and the decision threshold for triggering investigation; the logging pipeline is then configured to compute exactly those statistics in real time.\",\n      \"why\": \"This makes the knowledge frontier our compliance mechanism: every regulatory trigger becomes a published, replicable finding rather than an opaque internal alert.\"\n    }\n  ]\n}",
