-Source(1) Reference(2) Logging(3) Architecture(4) for(5) High-Risk(6) Systems(7) = 7 words. Good, under 10.\n\nWhat: We build and release an open-source logging middleware that any lab developing high-risk AI systems can integrate to meet Article 12's requirements while exposing a richer, scientifically useful event schema than the legal minimum demands. The codebase will be maintained as a living reference implementation.\n\nHow: A three-person engineering team will prototype the middleware against our own system stack over two quarters, then open-source it under an EU-compatible licence with documentation written jointly by engineers and researchers to make the scientific rationale for each logged field transparent.\n\nWhy: Releasing this tool multiplies the lab's broader scientific impact beyond its own systems, seeds a community conversation about what constitutes adequate technical documentation under Article 12, and establishes our institution as the reference point others cite when implementing compliant-by-design AI pipelines.\n\nWord count:\nTitle: Open-Source(1) Reference(2) Logging(3) Architecture(4) for(5) High-Risk(6) Systems(7) = 7 words\n\nWhat: We(1) build(2) and(3) release(4) an(5) open-source(6) logging(7) middleware(8) that(9) any(10) lab(11) developing(12) high-risk(13) AI(14) systems(15) can(16) integrate(17) to(18) meet(19) Article(20) 12's(21) requirements(22) while(23) exposing(24) a(25) richer(26), scientifically(27) useful(28) event(29) schema(30) than(31) the(32) legal(33) minimum(34) demands(35). The(36) codebase(37) will(38) be(39) maintained(40) as(41) a(42) living(43) reference(44) implementation(45). = 45 words\n\nHow: A(1) three-person(2) engineering(3) team(4) will(5) prototype(6) the(7) middleware(8) against(9) our(10) own(11) system(12) stack(13) over(14) two(15) quarters(16), then(17) open-source(18) it(19) under(20) an(21) EU-compatible(22) licence(23) with(24) documentation(25) written(26) jointly(27) by(28) engineers(29) and(