h Labs\" (8 words) ✓\nWhat: We build and maintain an open-source middleware library that wraps any high-risk model pipeline with Article 12-compliant automatic logging—capturing use periods, reference database versions, matched inputs, and verification personnel IDs as structured, queryable records. This is infrastructure work rather than a new model.\nHow: A small engineering-research team will implement the framework in Python and ONNX-compatible layers, release it on GitHub under an EU-friendly license, write integration guides for common lab stacks, and solicit contributions from partner labs to validate across architectures.\nWhy: Open tooling lowers the barrier for the broader scientific community to produce compliant research artifacts, amplifies our intellectual influence through adoption, and generates real-world usage data that feeds back into frontier research on logging efficiency.\n\nLet me count:\nWhat: We(1) build(2) and(3) maintain(4) an(5) open-source(6) middleware(7) library(8) that(9) wraps(10) any(11) high-risk(12) model(13) pipeline(14) with(15) Article(16) 12-compliant(17) automatic(18) logging—capturing(19) use(20) periods(21), reference(22) database(23) versions(24), matched(25) inputs(26), and(27) verification(28) personnel(29) IDs(30) as(31) structured(32), queryable(33) records(34). This(35) is(36) infrastructure(37) work(38) rather(39) than(40) a(41) new(42) model(43). = 43 words\n\nHow: A(1) small(2) engineering-research(3) team(4) will(5) implement(6) the(7) framework(8) in(9) Python(10) and(11) ONNX-compatible(12) layers(13), release(14) it(15) on(16) GitHub(17) under(18) an(19) EU-friendly(20) license(21), write(22) integration(23) guides(24) for(25) common(26) lab(27) stacks(28), and(29) solicit(30) contributions(31) from(32) partner(33) labs(34) to(35) validate(36) across(37) architectures(38). = 38 words\n\nWhy: Open(1) tooling(2) lowers(3) the(4) barrier(5) for(6) the(7) broader(8) scientific(9) community(10) to(11) produce(12) co