hy: \"It converts Article 12 from a per-project engineering tax into one infrastructure investment amortised across every high-risk deployment, protecting research headcount for actual science.\" (~26 words)\n\nTotal: 9 + 32 + 31 + 26 = 98. Good, within range.\n\n**Proposal 2: Compliance-Weighted Portfolio Re-scoring for Next Funding Cycle**\n- title: \"Compliance-Cost Weighting in Project Prioritisation Matrix\" (7 words) ✓\n- what: A re-scoring of every active and proposed R&D project using a new compliance-overhead coefficient that factors in logging complexity, Annex III category severity, and documentation-maintenance burden per research phase.\n- how: I would direct my programme managers to attach a 0–1 overhead multiplier to each project's resource estimate before next quarter's funding round, so biometric-ID work (Annex III 1(a)) with its heavier data-capture duties gets explicitly priced against less-burdensome high-risk lines.\n- why: It ensures we do not silently absorb compliance costs into research budgets until they crowd out the scientific milestones that justify our existence in the first place.\n\nCount: title(7) + what(~35) + how(~42) + why(~29) = ~113. Slightly over. Trim.\n\n- what: \"A re-scoring of every active and proposed R&D project using a compliance-overhead coefficient that factors logging complexity, Annex III category severity, and documentation-maintenance burden.\" (~27 words)\n- how: \"I would direct programme managers to attach an overhead multiplier to each resource estimate before next quarter's funding round, so biometric-ID work under Annex III 1(a) is explicitly priced against lighter high-risk lines.\" (~35 words)\n- why: \"It prevents compliance costs from silently eroding research budgets until they crowd out the scientific milestones that justify our lab's continued funding.\" (~23 words)\n\nTotal: 7 + 27 + 35 + 23 = 92. Good.\n\n**Proposal 3: Retrofit Existing Compute Clusters with Inherent Event-Recording**\n- title: \"Em