al Documentation and Traceability Governance\",\n\"what\": \"A standing internal function that owns the continuous updating of technical documentation — covering algorithms, training data, testing processes, and risk-management records — so that compliance evidence is current throughout each system's lifetime as Recital 71 requires.\",\n\"how\": \"We assign a dedicated documentation steward to every high-risk product line who runs quarterly refresh cycles tied to model retraining events and any substantial-modification triggers under Article 79(1).\",\n\"why\": \"Institutional survival depends on demonstrable, up-to-date traceability; this removes the chronic risk of stale documentation surfacing during a post-market monitoring inspection.\"\n},\n{\n\"title\": \"Annex III Biometric Product Compliance Roadmap\",\n\"what\": \"A strategic review and re-prioritisation of our biometric identification pipeline to ensure every product in the Annex III(1)(a) category is designed from inception around the four specific logging minimums — usage periods, reference databases, matched inputs, and verifier identity records.\",\n\"how\": \"The product strategy team conducts a gap assessment against Article 12(3) for each biometric project, then sequences development so that logging capabilities ship with version one rather than as a patch after market entry.\",\n\"why\": \"Market reputation in the EU hinges on being seen as a compliant vendor; shipping logging-native products differentiates us and protects our commercial licence to operate.\"\n}\n]\n}",
