rrent and future high-risk projects, protecting limited lab budget from redundant per-system logging builds.\"\n},\n{\n\"title\": \"Compliance Cost Centre in R&D Budget\",\n\"what\": \"A dedicated funding line item that pools the recurring costs of documentation upkeep, log retention, and lifetime monitoring across all active high-risk system projects rather than letting each principal investigator absorb them separately.\",\n\"how\": \"I will restructure next fiscal year's allocation to reserve roughly eight per cent of total R&D spend in this shared centre, drawing on existing administrative staff and our current data-centre contracts instead of new hires or external vendor agreements.\",\n\"why\": \"It converts a variable, project-level compliance burden into a predictable fixed cost, letting PIs plan ambitious science without fear of unbudgeted regulatory overhead derailing their work.\"\n},\n{\n\"title\": \"Research-Byproduct Documentation Templates for Article 12\",\n\"what\": \"Standardised auto-generated technical-documentation templates that pull directly from our experiment-tracking tools—hyperparameters, dataset hashes, validation curves—so the Recital 71 documentation is produced as a natural output of every training run.\",\n\"how\": \"The data-engineering group extends our internal MLflow-based tracker to emit structured compliance artefacts at each pipeline stage (training, testing, validation), eliminating the separate documentation-writing step that currently consumes two postdocs per quarter.\",\n\"why\": \"It keeps technical documentation current without diverting scarce researcher-hours from novel science, directly addressing our core tension between scientific ambition and regulatory bookkeeping.\"\n}\n]\n}",
