y of our models.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"Embedding Compliance Documentation into the Research Pipeline\",\n      \"what\": \"We would restructure our internal R&D workflow so that every model iteration automatically produces the technical documentation and event logs specified by Article 12, rather than treating compliance as a post-hoc step before deployment.\",\n      \"how\": \"Engineering and research teams would co-design a CI/CD hook that triggers log generation, metadata capture covering training-data provenance and test-validation traces, risk-management annotations, and versioned documentation assembly at each pipeline stage.\",\n      \"why\": \"This removes the intellectual friction between rigorous science and regulatory accountability, ensuring our publications and deployed systems share a single auditable evidence trail without slowing discovery.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"Open-Source Benchmark Suite for High-Risk AI Log Fidelity\",\n      \"what\": \"We would build and release a public benchmark that scores how faithfully different logging implementations capture the events Article 12(2)(a) through (c) requires, giving the scientific community a shared yardstick for traceability engineering.\",\n      \"how\": \"The lab would define evaluation metrics covering completeness, temporal resolution, and data-fidelity under privacy constraints, implement them as containerized test harnesses, validate against three open high-risk model families, then publish the suite on an open repository.\",\n      \"why\": \"This extends our scientific impact beyond internal deliverables by establishing a community-standard measurement tool that other labs, regulators, and auditors can adopt to benchmark their own systems.\"\n    }\n  ]\n}",
