onal survival by eliminating the most common cause of non-compliance — after-the-fact documentation gaps that regulators cannot accept.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"Pre-Deployment Traceability Audit Gate\",\n      \"what\": \"A standing compliance checkpoint in the R&D lifecycle where no high-risk system may be released until an independent review confirms its logging capabilities satisfy Articles 12(1), 12(2)(a)–(c), and, where applicable, the minimum fields of Article 12(3).\",\n      \"how\": \"Two senior engineers and the Compliance Officer form a three-person gate panel; each system submission must include a traceability matrix mapping every log event to its regulatory basis, validated in staging against adversarial failure scenarios.\",\n      \"why\": \"This gates market-entry risk at the cheapest possible point, preserving both our regulatory standing and the lab's reputation with enterprise customers who will demand audit-ready systems before signing.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"Lifetime-Scale Log Retention and Retrieval Infrastructure\",\n      \"what\": \"A dedicated, tamper-evident data store designed to hold every event log for the full operational lifetime of each high-risk system, with structured retrieval that satisfies Article 12(3) minimums for biometric-identification systems under Annex III point 1(a).\",\n      \"how\": \"We will procure a write-once-read-many storage solution co-managed with our IT security team, implement automated integrity checks quarterly, and draft standard operating procedures for regulator-facing log production within forty-eight hours of a request.\",\n      \"why\": \"Long-term retention capability is the difference between demonstrating compliance and failing an on-site inspection, directly safeguarding the lab's licence to operate in EU markets.\"\n    }\n  ]\n}",
