tems from scratch.\"\n},\n{\n\"title\": \"Embed Compliance Gates in the R&D Pipeline\",\n\"what\": \"We would restructure our project lifecycle so Article 12 logging specifications become acceptance criteria at the design phase, with each high-risk system proposal requiring a traceability architecture sketch before engineering begins.\",\n\"how\": \"Research managers must add a one-page logging specification to every initiation document, reviewed by compliance before model training starts; in-progress projects get a 90-day transition window. This adds two days per cycle but eliminates costly late-stage rework.\",\n\"why\": \"Front-loading avoids retrofitting traceability onto architectures never designed for it, protecting both funding timelines and scientific momentum.\"\n},\n{\n\"title\": \"Develop a Domain-Specific Traceability Logging Framework\",\n\"what\": \"We would develop and open-source a lightweight logging framework purpose-built for AI system lifetime event capture, turning the compliance requirement into reusable IP other labs in our sector can adopt or license from us.\",\n\"how\": \"Two senior researchers allocated 30% time over twelve months would design the schema using our existing deployment telemetry as test cases, publishing a specification paper alongside the code. This runs parallel to core model research without competing for the same engineers.\",\n\"why\": \"A public framework positions our lab as the sector's compliance reference point, strengthening grant applications and EU funding calls where regulatory readiness is an explicit criterion.\"\n}\n]\n}",
